========================================================================

  s(k) = savings fraction at level k:

  k: 1.0000 0.7500 0.6038 0.5077 0.4396 0.3889 0.3495 0.3180 0.2922 0.2706 0.2523 0.2365 0.2228 0.2107 0.2000 0.1904 0.1818 0.1740 0.1669 

  Savings INCREASE with k: True
  Wait — savings should DECREASE with k (larger k = more bits = less constrained)
  Let me check: k=1: s=1.0000, k=2: s=0.7500, k=10: s=0.2706
  Actually: savings DECREASE from 1.00 (k=1) toward ~0.12 (k=19)
  This is correct: smaller sub-tournaments are more constrained.


